<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $161.4 mln Sept 18.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $161.4 mln Sept 18.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $161.4 million surplus on Sept 18 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 18</p>
<p>Exports: $272.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $162.6 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $193.3 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $141.5 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $161.4 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.851 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.087 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.909 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.446 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $227 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
